To decompose the mission description into a goal model for a multi-robot system, we need to identify the main objectives and break them down into sub-goals and tasks. Here's how the goal model can be structured:

### Goal Model

#### Goals

| Name | Text | Runtime | Goal Type | Relation |
|------|------|---------|-----------|----------|
| G1: Mission Execution | Execute the mission of collecting and delivering resources | - | Perform | AND |
| G2: Resource Collection | Collect required resources from storage | FALLBACK(G3, G4) | Achieve | OR |
| G3: Single Storage Collection | Collect resources from a single storage location | - | Achieve | - |
| G4: Multi-Storage Collection | Collect resources from multiple storages | # | Achieve | AND |
| G5: Resource Delivery | Deliver collected resources to the specified location | - | Perform | AND |
| G6: Battery Management | Manage battery levels during mission | FALLBACK(G7, G8) | Achieve | OR |
| G7: Recharge During Collection | Recharge if battery < 10% during collection | - | Achieve | - |
| G8: Recharge During Delivery | Return to checkpoint if battery < 30% during delivery | - | Achieve | - |

#### Tasks

| Name | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots |
|------|------|----------|----------|------------------|
| AT1: Navigate to Storage | Navigate to the specified storage location | AND | Storage | [1,2] |
| AT2: Request Resources | Send message to storage for resource retrieval | AND | Storage | 1 |
| AT3: Retrieve Resources | Wait and retrieve resources from storage | AND | Storage | 1 |
| AT4: Deliver Resources | Deliver resources to the specified location | AND | Delivery Location | [1,2] |
| AT5: Monitor Battery | Monitor battery level during mission | AND | Any | 1 |
| AT6: Recharge Robot | Recharge robot at station | AND | Recharging Station | 1 |
| AT7: Assign Mission to Another Robot | Assign remaining task to another robot | AND | Any | 1 |
| AT8: Trigger Alert | Trigger alert for failure to return resource | AND | Any | 1 |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G5, G6 [AND]**
  - The mission execution requires both resource collection and delivery, along with battery management.

- **G2 -> G3, G4 [OR]**
  - Resource collection can be from a single storage or multiple storages.

- **G4 -> AT1, AT2, AT3 [AND]**
  - Multi-storage collection involves navigating to storage, requesting resources, and retrieving them.

- **G5 -> AT4 [AND]**
  - Resource delivery involves delivering resources to the specified location.

- **G6 -> G7, G8 [OR]**
  - Battery management involves handling low battery during collection or delivery.

- **G7 -> AT5, AT6 [AND]**
  - Recharging during collection involves monitoring battery and recharging if necessary.

- **G8 -> AT5, AT4, AT7, AT8 [AND]**
  - Recharging during delivery involves monitoring battery, delivering resources, assigning tasks, and triggering alerts if needed.

This goal model provides a structured approach to decomposing the mission into actionable tasks and goals, ensuring efficient execution by multiple robots.
